    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Community-Director--Village-A_JR27280-1": {
      "title": "Community Director, Village A",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Community Director in Residential Education at Georgetown University administers the residential program for a campus community housing between 225-600 students. The Community Director’s primary role is to foster the holistic development of students through active engagement and mentoring of students in the residential education experience. Duties include supervision and development of the Resident Assistant or Resident Fellow staff and the design of cultural, educational, and social programming supporting the formation of students in the Jesuit tradition. The Community Director, in partnership with the Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, educates students through the development of Educational Plans, promotion of leadership development, partnerships with Faculty and Resident Ministers, emergency response, and through community investment in an established code that emphasizes respect for self and others.  The Community Director manages the occupancy, safety, and security of the residential area they oversee. The Community Director is a critical member of Georgetown’s Safety Net and works closely with the Georgetown University Police Department and other Student Affairs offices to respond to student emergencies, including mental health crises, facility emergencies, injury, and other concerns. The Community Director serves on an emergency response duty rotation and responds to significant student issues. During the summer months, Community Directors play a vital role in creating and planning departmental programs and services while supporting the residential conference and intern housing operations. Community Directors are expected to serve as positive ambassadors of the University and Residential Living mission, vision, and values within their teams, communities, and across campus. The Community Director primarily performs desk work in an office or workspace using a university issued computer. Some meetings or events occur in other buildings on the Hilltop or Capitol Campus or occasionally at off campus locations. This position is required to live on campus and participate in an on-call/on-site duty rotation 24-hours a day, 365 days a year. The Community Director must be able to respond quickly to emergencies (behavioral, health related, and facility/physical plant) and other needs when they arise. Work Interactions Community Directors supervise the student Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow team and lead all community development and student formation initiatives within their assigned community. The Community Director provides mediation services to students, supervision to Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, developmental guidance to students, and feedback to departmental leadership. On a daily basis the Community Director schedules student meetings and is readily available to student staff and colleagues. The Community Director is expected to communicate in a timely manner with faculty, staff, parents, and others regarding shared concerns about students.  Requirements and Qualifications A completed Master's Degree is required, preferably in the area of Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or Social Work. Thorough understanding of and commitment to the work of Residential Living as well as the education and character development of college students is expected. Demonstrated experience in the areas of leadership, supervision, professional development, administrative skills, social justice and inclusion, community development, educational engagement, and emergency response. Ability to manage stress, conflict, and frustration constructively; demonstrate a positive attitude. Identify, define, and apply creative and original approaches to resolving issues and use sound judgment based on training and departmental policies and protocol. An awareness and understanding of the Jesuit values and the ability to conceptualize them in the application of this role. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Emergency Employee This position has been designated as an emergency position. Because many services provided by the University are required seven days a week on a twenty-four hour basis, the University makes every effort to remain open at all times. This position must always report to work on time regardless of weather conditions, whether the University is closed or not. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $41,926.00 - $65,090.00 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Healy-4th-Floor/Director-for-Finance-and-Operations---Georgetown-University_JR27262": {
      "title": "Director for Finance and Operations - Georgetown University",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview This position is responsible for all aspects of budget and financial operations for one of the two large groups of clusters of Main Campus Administrative Units. The incumbent will hold a key position on the Main Campus Administrative Units Finance Team, reporting directly to the Senior Business Manager (“SBM”).  He/she has a direct oversight of a Sr. Financial Analyst and an indirect oversight of an Associate Director of Finance & Ops.  Director is responsible for all annual budget activities, including top-down and detailed budget development and forecasting, for monitoring the actual performance of the units against the budget, for financial operations, and for the year-end close activities for the assigned units with an annual expense budget exceeding $70M. In addition, responsibilities include review and oversight of HCM transactions as a Finance Partner (in conjunction and under guidance of the Senior Business Manager), planning for and monitoring of the restricted funds and research expenditures as directed by the SMB and the CFO of Main Campus. The Director will work with procurement and or accountants on a regular basis. Work Interactions The Director for Finance & Ops will report directly to the Senior Business Manager (SBM) for the Administrative Units on Main Campus and will work closely with the SBM on operational, planning and strategic matters of the units he/she is responsible for.  The position holder will be in close contact with the Unit Heads that his/her team supports. This position interacts with many university departments, which requires excellent customer service and communication skills and the ability to work with a wide range of constituents, such as Deans, Vice Provosts, Department heads, faculty, the Joint Office of Research Administration, Advancement, and various offices under the OCFO, for example, Accounts Payable, Payroll Services, General Accounting, and other.  The incumbent works closely with the Provost Office Finance Team. The Director will regularly collaborate with other Associate Directors, Directors and SBMs from Schools and be part of the Main Campus Financial Operations Working Group.  The incumbent will interact with the Campus CFO and other leaders of Main Campus.  Requirements and Qualifications A Bachelor’s degree is required.  Master’s degree in economics, finance, business or accounting is strongly preferred.  A Bachelor’s degree plus substantial experience in closely related fields may substitute for a Master’s degree. 10+ years' of progressive work experience in financial analysis and budgeting in a sophisticated office environment. Relevant financial acumen (budgeting, transactional support, revenue-generating activities, chart of accounts, journals, requisitions, purchase orders, procurement, and travel) Ability to build and utilize financial reports Advanced business analytics skills Ability to support the establishment and management of budgets of $70M+ Strong leadership skills coupled with proven team management abilities. Prior experience working with complex teams Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills Ability to engage regularly with internal and external stakeholders, including unit leads and administrators across the institution Strong organizational and time management skills; proficiency managing and prioritizing multiple tasks Ability to work with a variety of financial systems, with prior experience preferred in Workday, and Adaptive Ability to interpret the strategic goals and plan for assigned units Revenue and expenditure analysis experience Prior experience with complex financial and longitudinal planning and financial forecasting Adaptability and flexibility Attention to detail Ability to triage and solve complex challenges and requests Proficiency in the Microsoft Office suite, with a mastery of excel and experience with managing and analyzing large volumes of data Service oriented, professional demeanor and a team orientation is required; i.e. avoiding “that’s not my job” Ability to work well under pressure, in a high paced environment Ability to think outside the box and to solve problems creatively Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Telework. The work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $80,429.00 - $157,238.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Graduate-Program-Coordinator--Department-of-Government---Georgetown-University-College-of-Arts---Sciences_JR27245": {
      "title": "Graduate Program Coordinator, Department of Government - Georgetown University College of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Graduate Program Coordinator (a one-year renewable term position) is responsible for supporting the academic, administrative, operational, enrollment management, and strategic communication functions of assigned graduate programs within the College of Arts and Sciences, primarily but not limited to the M.A. in Conflict Resolution. The Graduate Program Coordinator reports to the Business Manager with a dotted line to the Program Director and collaborates closely with faculty, university offices, students, alumni, and external stakeholders to advance program goals and operations. This position serves as a key operational and strategic partner in managing the day-to-day functions of assigned programs, with responsibilities spanning enrollment management, admissions and merit aid administration, marketing and communications, student and faculty support, event coordination, and program operations. The incumbent designs and implements recruitment and yield strategies to support enrollment goals, manages admissions workflows and communications, and oversees digital outreach efforts including website management, social media, marketing materials, and public relations initiatives to raise program visibility and engagement. The role also requires awareness of financial policies, program expenditures, and the operational implications of budget-related decisions associated with events, financial aid, and other program activities. In collaboration with the department’s Administrative Coordinator, the Graduate Program Coordinator also supports academic and administrative operations by coordinating course scheduling and registration processes, assisting with program assessment and reporting, supporting research and student engagement activities, and ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. In addition, the position plans and executes special events such as orientations, commencement activities, academic programming, alumni engagement events, and recruitment initiatives while monitoring budgets and operational logistics. The role requires strong collaboration, organizational, communication, analytical, and project management skills, as well as the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic academic environment. Duties may also include broader program support functions related to alumni relations, community development, and other operational needs as assigned by program leadership. Work Interactions This position reports to the Department Business Manager and Program Director and works closely with the department’s staff, faculty, students, and alumni. The incumbent will call, email, and meet with prospective and current students. They will work closely with all functional areas within the College Dean’s Office staff as well as prospective students, current students, alumni, vendors/suppliers, industry connections, and many other audiences. The incumbent will liaise with other Georgetown University offices such as Graduate Admissions, University Registrar, Office of Global Services, Student Financial Services and Financial Affairs and other academic units. The incumbent should demonstrate a proactive and adaptable approach to their work, remaining responsive to the evolving needs of the program and university community. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. 2-3 years of relevant experience, preferably in higher education. Commitment to student success as part of an equitable and diverse community. Working knowledge of enrollment management and admissions best practices. Exceptional communication skills in writing, editing, public speaking, and customer service. Strong analytical, financial, and documentation skills; experience using data to understand historical trends to drive and support decision making, linking strategies to outcomes. A self-starter with a proven ability to collaborate and develop best-in-class business models, systems, and procedures to support an exceptional student experience. Events management experience. An ability to understand the nuanced needs and characteristics of this specialized academic program, and the ability to authentically articulate the unique opportunities and value. Understanding of social media and emerging media tools to utilize in recruitment and branding of the program. Organized, and proactive; highly responsive, flexible, and adaptable.  Technical aptitude and the ability to pick up new technology quickly.     Understanding of appropriate and confidential communication, file management, and storage. Proficiency with Google Apps, WordPress or other web editing tools, and the Adobe Suite (Acrobat, Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, and Premier Pro) Preferred Qualifications Experience in graduate program management. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Cover letter and resume required for consideration. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
