    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Zero-Waste-and-Special-Projects-Coordinator-_JR27437": {
      "title": "Zero Waste and Special Projects Coordinator,",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Located in a historic neighborhood in the nation's capital, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, with a global perspective. Our community is composed of remarkable individuals interested in intellectual inquiry and making a difference in the world. The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects contributes to the ongoing optimization of Georgetown University’s Zero Waste initiatives at the Hilltop and Capitol Campuses. Additionally, the Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects supports efforts to achieve Georgetown’s sustainability strategic plan through special projects. Reporting directly to Manager, Administration and Analysis, Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects interacts with faculty, staff, unionized employees, students, senior leadership, neighbors, external partners, vendors, and government agencies to implement strategic initiatives and drive behavior change in our campus communities.   Work Interactions Georgetown University is committed to addressing critical sustainability challenges through research, teaching, and institutional practices. The University is taking an integrated and holistic approach to sustainability, guided by its Jesuit values, and its commitment to justice and the common good.   Through engagement and strategic planning, the Office of Sustainability fosters a culture of sustainability at Georgetown, bridging practice with learning and research, while supporting the university in taking institutional action on issues related to sustainability on campus, in administrative operations, and in the local community.   The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects supports initiatives and projects that drive progress towards the university’s zero waste performance targets and the university’s overall sustainability goals. The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects reports to the Manager, Administration and Analysis in the Office of Sustainability. The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects aids the Manager, Administration and Analysis in the convening and facilitation of cross-functional teams working together to achieve the university’s sustainability goals. The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects role is also embedded in the Waste Management functions reporting to the Solid Waste Disposal & Recycling Manager in Planning, Facilities, and Management. The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects works between the Office of Sustainability and Planning, Facilities, and Management to align programming and ensure operational efficiency. The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects works on behalf of the Office of Sustainability and Planning, Facilities, and Management interacting regularly with key university stakeholders and providing guidance and educational training on sustainability related matters.   The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects plays a key role in supporting the Manager, Administration and Analysis with data collection and analysis from internal partners for internal and external reporting purposes.   Requirements and Qualifications The Coordinator, Zero Waste and Special Projects must have the demonstrated ability to form trusted and effective relationships and partnerships, and the ability to manage such partnerships in a way that leads to mutual benefit in the implementation of sustainability programs and projects.   This position requires a bachelor’s degree in environmental science or a related discipline. The ideal candidate will have a minimum of two years of experience contributing to progressively complex project implementation in an environmental science focused organization, higher education preferred. The candidate must have demonstrated experience supporting and collaborating with senior leadership. Excellent written and oral communication skills, including grammar, spelling and composition are necessary. The candidate must have exceptionally strong organizational skills and must also demonstrate proven interpersonal skills in a high-profile environment with courtesy, professionalism, diplomacy, and efficiency. Analytical abilities required, with demonstrated experience collecting, analyzing, and reporting data from sustainability functional areas (e.g. sustainable built environment, sustainable food systems, inclusive sustainability, water resources, clean energy, urban biodiversity, sustainable transportation, circularity of materials, regenerative economy). Must be able to effectively manage and prioritize multiple independent tasks.   This position requires proficiency in the use of standard office productivity software including Google Suite, Microsoft Office Suite, and the ability to compose clear and compelling presentations and other correspondence (utilizing Powerpoint, Google Slides, Canva, Presi, or other Presentation Programs).   The ideal candidate is extremely organized, flexible and creative, and able to work with a variety of personalities and constituencies to meet the demands of the job. The candidate is a proactive self-starter who will also take direction and feedback from supervisors to adjust their approach to the work. The candidate proactively engages with, learns and communicates with evolving technologies to enhance the productivity of the Office of Sustainability team. The ideal candidate will be a trusted member of an essential team.   Additionally, it is preferred that the ideal candidate hold a TRUE Zero Waste Advisor and/or LEED GREEN Associate or other relevant sustainability credential. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Executive-Coordinator--Office-of-the-Senior-Vice-President-for-Strategic-Engagement---Georgetown-University_JR27420": {
      "title": "Executive Coordinator, Office of the Senior Vice President for Strategic Engagement – Georgetown University",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Executive Coordinator , Office of the Senior Vice President for Strategic Engagement – Georgetown University. The Office of the Senior Vice President for Strategic Engagement (SVP) is seeking a proactive, highly organized, and collaborative Executive Coordinator to assist with a wide range of administrative tasks and projects covering a variety of functional areas. The Office of the Senior Vice President’s portfolio includes oversight of the Department of Intercollegiate Athletics, Office of Public Affairs, Office of Government Affairs and Community Engagement, Office of Global Engagement, Initiative on Catholic Social Thought and Public Life, and the Center for the Study of Slavery and Its Legacies. This role serves as a key administrative and operational position for the SVP, ensuring seamless execution of day-to-day operations including scheduling and calendar management, meeting facilitation, priorities management, and high-level internal and external stakeholder engagement.  In addition, the Executive Coordinator will engage in research, writing, and independent project management as needed.    As a dynamic and cross-functional team member, the Executive Coordinator works to anticipate needs, process sensitive information with strict confidentiality, and ensure smooth workflow in the office of the SVP.  Additionally, this role supports regular annual meetings and events and well as special projects as assigned.   The successful candidate is independent, self-motivated, agile, and possesses superior judgement and discretion. The Executive Coordinator must have a dedication to creative thinking and independent problem solving, and must be willing to work occasional early mornings, evenings, and weekends. This position puts a premium on initiative, versatility, good judgment, problem-solving, excellent interpersonal and communications skills, and a positive, can-do attitude.    Duties include but are not limited to: Managing the SVP’s day-to-day schedule, to include scheduling appointment and meetings, resolving conflicting priorities, and ensuring meeting timeliness. Manage routine business processes, including invoice and expense processing, booking travel, and arranging catering. Preparing briefings and presentations for the SVP on issue areas and in advance of key meetings. Conducting research and gathering data for the SVP and SVP’s team as directed. Independent project management as directed.   Requirements and Qualifications This position requires a bachelor’s degree and three to five years of progressively complex administrative and customer service experience supporting senior leaders. Candidate must have exceptionally strong organizational skills and analytical abilities, and must also demonstrate proven interpersonal skills and experience providing complex administrative support in a high profile environment with courtesy, professionalism, diplomacy, efficiency and confidentiality. Must be able to effectively manage and prioritize multiple tasks, understand stakeholder needs, and work under pressure. This position requires proficiency in the use of standard office equipment such as printers, copiers, faxes, and scanners as well as excellent skills with standard office productivity software including Gmail, Google Calendaring and other applications, Microsoft Office Suite (MSWord, Excel, Outlook and PowerPoint), including the use of advanced formatting of Word, the ability to set up and use Excel spreadsheets. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .   Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
