    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Downtown-Campus/Operations-Coordinator_JR27401-1": {
      "title": "Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview This position serves as an Operations Coordinator for the Capitol Campus. Georgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and The Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world.   The Operations Coordinator provides critical customer service as well as support for facilities, security and guest services coordination at the Level 1 reception desk of 111 Massachusetts Ave. The position provides hands-on, in-person interactions and requires excellent customer service skills while interfacing with staff, students, faculty and visitors of the Capitol Campus.   The incumbent will work closely with the other Operations Team members to ensure support and transparent transitions for external guests and students. The position requires intimate knowledge of all programming offered at the Capitol Campus, daily operations, security protocols, and will serve as liaison to staff, students, faculty and visitors at 111 Mass. The position may require light manual labor. Basic knowledge of facilities maintenance is desired. Reporting directly to the Senior Director of Operations for the Capitol Campus, this position supports Georgetown’s goal of high stakeholder satisfaction. The Operations Coordinator supports the Operations Team on all aspects of successful campus-wide operations, focused specifically on making sure customer service and security is provided at the highest level during all shifts.   Work Interactions and Work Mode Designation ● Daily interaction with other Operations Coordinators, Sr. Director of Operations, GU staff, students, faculty and visitors; ● Close collaboration and communication with GUPD; ● Communication with facility vendors and housekeeping staff; ● GU Leadership   This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .   Requirements and Qualifications ● High School Diploma and up to 2 years of relevant experience required, or equivalent combination of education and relevant work experience. Bachelor’s degree preferred; ● Two to four years of progressive administrative experience in educational setting preferred; ● Demonstrated ability to provide very high levels of customer service, professionalism and time management skills; ● Knowledge of University offices, computers and financial systems is desired; ● Proficient in Microsoft Office and comfortable responding to telephone and email inquiries; ● Familiarity with Google Workspace tools (Gmail, Google Drive, etc.); ● This position must also demonstrate proficiency in the use of University protocols and student policies; ● The ideal person will have strong problem-solving skills, time management skills, attention to detail, strong oral and written communications skills, enthusiasm and ability to work effectively under pressure. This individual must be a detail-oriented team player and able to manage multiple tasks. ● Strong interpersonal skills required. A friendly, helpful demeanor along with a willingness to enforce the University’s policies are crucial for this role.   Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $19.20 - $28.70 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Community-Director--McCarthy-Hall_JR27283": {
      "title": "Community Director, McCarthy Hall",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements The Community Director in Residential Education at Georgetown University administers the residential program for a campus community housing between 225-600 students. The Community Director’s primary role is to foster the holistic development of students through active engagement and mentoring of students in the residential education experience. Duties include supervision and development of the Resident Assistant or Resident Fellow staff and the design of cultural, educational, and social programming supporting the formation of students in the Jesuit tradition. The Community Director, in partnership with the Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, educates students through the development of Educational Plans, promotion of leadership development, partnerships with Faculty and Resident Ministers, emergency response, and through community investment in an established code that emphasizes respect for self and others. The Community Director manages the occupancy, safety, and security of the residential area they oversee. The Community Director is a critical member of Georgetown’s Safety Net and works closely with the Georgetown University Police Department and other Student Affairs offices to respond to student emergencies, including mental health crises, facility emergencies, injury, and other concerns. The Community Director serves on an emergency response duty rotation and responds to significant student issues. During the summer months, Community Directors play a vital role in creating and planning departmental programs and services while supporting the residential conference and intern housing operations. Community Directors are expected to serve as positive ambassadors of the University and Residential Living mission, vision, and values within their teams, communities, and across campus. The Community Director primarily performs desk work in an office or workspace using a university issued computer. Some meetings or events occur in other buildings on the Hilltop or Capitol Campus or occasionally at off campus locations. This position is required to live on campus and participate in an on-call/on-site duty rotation 24-hours a day, 365 days a year. The Community Director must be able to respond quickly to emergencies (behavioral, health related, and facility/physical plant) and other needs when they arise. Work Interactions Community Directors supervise the student Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow team and lead all community development and student formation initiatives within their assigned community. The Community Director provides mediation services to students, supervision to Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, developmental guidance to students, and feedback to departmental leadership. On a daily basis the Community Director schedules student meetings and is readily available to student staff and colleagues. The Community Director is expected to communicate in a timely manner with faculty, staff, parents, and others regarding shared concerns about students.  Requirements and Qualifications A completed Master's Degree is required, preferably in the area of Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or Social Work. Thorough understanding of and commitment to the work of Residential Living as well as the education and character development of college students is expected. Demonstrated experience in the areas of leadership, supervision, professional development, administrative skills, social justice and inclusion, community development, educational engagement, and emergency response. Ability to manage stress, conflict, and frustration constructively; demonstrate a positive attitude. Identify, define, and apply creative and original approaches to resolving issues and use sound judgment based on training and departmental policies and protocol. An awareness and understanding of the Jesuit values and the ability to conceptualize them in the application of this role. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Emergency Employee This position has been designated as an emergency position. Because many services provided by the University are required seven days a week on a twenty-four hour basis, the University makes every effort to remain open at all times. This position must always report to work on time regardless of weather conditions, whether the University is closed or not. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $41,926.00 - $65,090.00 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Associate-Director-of-Administration-and-Operations_JR27452": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Administration and Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Associate Director of Administration and Operations serves as the senior administrator responsible for the administrative and operational functions of the Office of Undergraduate Admissions. Reporting directly to the Dean of Admissions and serving as a member of the Office’s leadership team, the Associate Director provides executive-level administrative and operational support to the Dean and Senior Associate Directors while overseeing the systems, processes, personnel, and resources that support the work of the Office. The Associate Director manages and provides oversight for office operations, personnel administration, procurement, facilities coordination, administrative services, records and workflow management, and other operational functions. The position supervises administrative staff, establishes priorities and expectations, develops and implements procedures, coordinates office-wide projects, and identifies opportunities to improve efficiency, consistency, and service. Working with a high degree of independence and professional judgment, the Associate Director anticipates operational needs, resolves administrative challenges, and ensures that day-to-day functions are effectively coordinated across the Office. The Associate Director also serves as a primary liaison between Undergraduate Admissions and University administrative departments, coordinating matters that require collaboration with Human Resources, Finance, Procurement, Facilities, Information Technology, and other campus partners. The position works closely with admissions leadership and staff to ensure that administrative resources and operational processes are aligned with the demands of the annual admissions cycle and evolving departmental priorities. Through this work, the Associate Director plays a critical role in maintaining the administrative infrastructure necessary for a complex, high-volume admissions operation. The position ensures that the Dean, leadership, admissions officers, and administrative staff have the operational support, resources, and processes necessary to carry out the Office’s responsibilities effectively and to advance the University’s undergraduate enrollment priorities. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Direct the administrative operations and business functions of the Office of Undergraduate Admissions Provide executive-level administrative support to the Dean of Admissions and Senior Associate Directors Manages 2 direct reports and 4 indirect reports Supervise administrative staff and oversee hiring, onboarding, performance management, and professional development Develop, implement, and evaluate administrative policies, procedures, and operational practices Oversee personnel administration, office operations, records management, procurement, facilities coordination, and administrative technology Manage administrative projects and operational initiatives that support departmental priorities Oversee the administrative resources that support recruitment activities, admissions programs, events, and strategic initiatives Serve as the Office's primary liaison with University administrative departments Oversee procurement, contracts, vendor relationships, budget monitoring, and stewardship of administrative resources Evaluate administrative processes and implement improvements that enhance service, efficiency, and compliance. Work Interactions The Associate Director reports directly to the Dean of Admissions and serves as a member of the Office's leadership team. The position works closely with the Dean, Senior Associate Directors, admissions officers, operations staff, and administrative personnel to establish administrative priorities and support departmental initiatives. The Associate Director directly supervises the Administrative Officer/Admissions Support Team Manager and the Assistant Director of Operations, providing leadership, coaching, performance management, and professional development. The position serves as the primary administrative liaison with Human Resources, Finance and Business Services, Procurement, University Information Services, Facilities Management, Payroll, Student Employment, University Events, the Office of the Provost, and other University departments. The Associate Director also works with vendors, alumni volunteers, prospective students, families, counselors, and other partners as needed to support Office operations. Requirements and Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Seven plus years of progressively responsible administrative or operational management experience Demonstrated experience supervising professional and administrative staff. Experience managing office operations, business processes, and administrative services. Excellent organizational, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and meet competing deadlines. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain confidentiality. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and enterprise administrative systems. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree strongly preferred Experience in higher education administration, admissions operations, enrollment management, or related academic environments Experience overseeing administrative operations, personnel coordination, or organizational workflow management Familiarity with HR-related administrative processes, staffing coordination, and operational planning Experience supporting high-volume operational environments with multiple functional areas and stakeholders Familiarity with Slate, Workday, Banner, Google Workspace, Microsoft Office applications, or similar operational systems Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $66,783.00 - $126,720.23 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Administrative-Project-Coordinator--Vice-Provost-for-Research_JR27423": {
      "title": "Administrative Project Coordinator, Vice Provost for Research",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview This position based in the Office of the Provost will provide direct administrative support to the Vice Provost for Research and to the Deputy to the Provost, and will complete additional tasks as assigned.  The individual must be organized, efficient, and able to coordinate multiple projects simultaneously.  S/he must be highly motivated, results-oriented, and pro-active in providing administrative, financial, and research support for the Office. This individual will prepare briefings, compose PowerPoint presentations, edit websites, send broadcast University mailings as needed, schedule, organize and manage meetings, projects, and events, execute related administrative functions, and stand in for the Special Assistant to the Provost in his/her absence.  The position requires superior organizational skills, a capacity to anticipate needs and to pre-emptively address them, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively with colleagues across the university. S/he will work in a team-oriented environment with the goal of ensuring the success of the Provost’s Office business and overall University initiatives. The work performed will be integral to the effective functioning of the Provost’s Office and its ability to implement projects, initiatives, and normal administrative duties throughout Main Campus.   Work Interactions The position will administratively report to the Vice Provost for Research, but will functionally report jointly to the Vice Provost for Research and the Deputy to the Provost, spending time working in each area.  The incumbent will interact closely with senior leaders in the Provost’s Office, and high-level stakeholders internally and externally including deans, faculty members, funding agencies, and others.  Requirements and Qualifications The successful candidate will possess the following qualifications: Superior written and verbal communication skills Outstanding organizational skills Exceptional reliability and work ethic Advanced Word, Excel PowerPoint, and web editing skills A familiarity with GMS an advantage A minimum of 1-3 years’ practical experience working in an administrative role preferable. Bachelor’s degree required. Advanced degree preferred. Experience working with senior leaders in a higher education setting preferable. Experience in managing multiple projects for multiple principals simultaneously.  Experience in working with Confidential Information Budgets/ Organization structures/ HR –related issues. High level of professionalism required. Experience in working on research administration issues and research grants a positive attribute. Experience working with funding agencies, including federal agencies, private foundations, and corporate sponsors, a positive attribute. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $20.16 - $31.30 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
