    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/111-Massachusetts-Ave-7th-Floor/Director-of-Programs-and-Student-Experience-McDonough-School-of-Business_JR27551": {
      "title": "Director of Programs and Student Experience-McDonough School of Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Director of Programs and Student Experience , Baratta Center for Global Business Education | McDonough School of Business - Georgetown University The Baratta Center for Global Business Education is Georgetown McDonough School of Business’s premier hub for training future global leaders at the intersection of business, policy, geopolitics, and technological change. This role leads the full student experience — designing and serving as the operational lead for the co-curricular programs, immersive global experiences, practitioner convenings, and internship placements that make the Baratta Center’s training transformative. It is a senior, high-ownership, entrepreneurial role with direct accountability to the Executive Director. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Co-Curricular Program Design and Execution Corporate Practitioner Integration into Programming Trek Development New Program Development and Innovation Student experience management Work Interactions The Director for Programs & Student Experience is the senior leader responsible for the Baratta Center's co-curricular programming portfolio, reporting directly to the Executive Director.  In close collaboration with the Executive Director, this role has ownership of what students experience as members of the Baratta Center community — from ideation and curriculum design through execution, assessment, and continuous improvement. It is a consequential role with high ambition and significant scope for creativity and innovation. Much of the Center's programming involves bringing corporate leaders, practitioners, government officials, and global executives into direct engagement with students — as instructors, case study subjects, mentors, and speakers. The Director works in close partnership with the Associate Director for External Relations to ensure that the right external voices are embedded in the right program formats. The Director leads the design and delivery of program; the External Relations AD leads the corporate relationship and the ask. These two roles are in constant collaboration.   Requirements and Qualifications MBA or equivalent advanced degree; 5-7 years of experience , ideally with private sector experience (eg consulting, corporate strategy, finance, or a related field) and exposure to public sector, policy, or government environments through work experience, graduate study, or sustained professional engagement. Demonstrated track record of designing and executing multi-stakeholder programs from concept through execution at a level of seniority commensurate with a director role. Substantive knowledge of, or professional engagement with, geopolitics or international business. Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to design curriculum, write intellectually rigorous program materials, and facilitate senior-level conversations. Proven ability to work with significant autonomy and exercise sound judgment in a fast-paced, resource-constrained environment. Deep familiarity with AI tools, proficiency with MS Word, Powerpoint , Excel. Experience designing or running programs in an academic, think tank, policy institute, or institutional setting preferred Teaching or facilitation experience in a professional or academic setting preferred Preferred qualifications Bachelor's degree with exceptional relevant experience considered.   Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid , with a minimum 60% on-campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $80,429.00 - $157,238.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
