    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Qatar/Director-of-Faculty-Affairs_JR27478-1": {
      "title": "Director of Faculty Affairs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Georgetown University in Qatar (GU-Q), located in Doha , is seeking Director of Faculty Affairs to oversee faculty recruitment, appointments, reappointments, promotions, and key academic administration and compliance processes. The role also serves as second-in-command to the Senior Associate Dean for Faculty and Academic Affairs, supporting academic decision-making, and departmental leadership. The position is for a 3 year term, eligible for renewal. Key Accountabilities: Oversee the processes for recruitment, appointment, reappointment, and promotion of full-time core and teaching faculty, and the recruitment and appointment of adjunct faculty. Communicate and advise faculty on relevant university policies and procedures, and assist the Associate Dean in tracking compliance. Oversee and coordinate a high volume of administrative processes, including those related to promotion, reappointment, research leave, faculty merit, overload teaching, and course banking. Serves as second-in-command to the Senior Associate Dean for Faculty and Academic Affairs, supporting high-level academic decision-making and departmental leadership.   Key Activities: In consultation with the Dean, Associate Dean, and Faculty Chair, coordinate full-time faculty searches and oversee recruitment processes. Manage the appointment processes for and support of visiting faculty, including from the main campus in Washington, DC, in consultation with curricular field chairs, the Faculty Chair, the Associate Dean, and the Dean. Recruit and hire adjunct instructors, in consultation with the Dean, Associate Dean, Faculty Chair, and curricular field chairs. Collaborate with other units to ensure the effective academic onboarding and orientation of new faculty. In consultation with the Associate Dean and Faculty Chair, review faculty travel requests. Oversee curricular activities fund and curricular group funding, ensuring usage of funds is in accordance with their respective policies. Collaborate with the Office of Research to manage certain administrative aspects of research programs and processes (including summer supplement), like collecting and tracking proposals and overseeing payouts. Support the Dean, Associate Dean, and Faculty Chair to ensure that all faculty meet workload standards. Work with the Office of the Dean, Faculty Chair, and Provost Office to ensure the timely and efficient initiation and completion of reappointment and promotion processes as mandated in the Faculty Framework. Manage collection of Faculty Annual Reports and work with faculty to secure  timely and complete submissions. Work with the Faculty Merit Committee to ensure timely reporting of annual faculty merit scores; work with HR to issue merit letters. Facilitate faculty requests for research leaves and, in collaboration with the Associate Dean and Faculty Chair, make sabbatical recommendations to the Dean; oversee issuance of leave letters. Oversee all curricular and faculty events. Support the Communications unit in collecting accurate data about faculty activities, publications, and research for public dissemination. Manage and oversee the work of direct reports, including setting and reviewing performance goals as well as identifying training and development needs. Liaise with Human Resources to manage recruitment, hiring, onboarding and offboarding of direct reports, as required. Respond to urgent requests and concerns via email, texts, and phone calls outside of normal working hours. Contribute to the curriculum by teaching when possible or necessary. Other similar duties as assigned.   Knowledge and Skills Familiarity with the culture of academia and research institutions. Ability to work collaboratively with diverse groups of faculty, staff, and other stakeholders across various cultural and institutional environments. Outstanding communication skills, including editing and writing. Excellent organizational, administrative, and coordination skills. Strong attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines. Proficiency in MS Office.   Qualifications Master’s degree preferably in the humanities or social sciences. PhD preferred.   Experience 8+ years of relevant work experience. Record of excellence in teaching, research, and service or significant experience as a senior academic administrator. Experience managing teams and working with university academic and administrative departments. Experience developing and implementing academic policies and procedures.      Expatriate Benefits and Relocation Support GU-Q offers a highly competitive expatriate benefits package including a monthly transportation and home leave travel allowance, worldwide health insurance, and generous private school tuition support for accompanying children, along with other benefits. Relocating to a new country can be a significant undertaking, and GU-Q is committed to providing comprehensive relocation support. This includes assistance with visa processing, arranging travel to Qatar, fully furnished temporary accommodation, transportation upon arrival, and campus orientation, helping new employees and their families settle into life in Qatar and the GU-Q community. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/111-Massachusetts-Ave-7th-Floor/Assistant-Director--Graduate---Executive-Degree-Programs-Admissions-McDonough-School-of-Business_JR27623": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Graduate & Executive Degree Programs Admissions-McDonough School of Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Assistant Director of Recruitment Graduate & Executive Degree Programs Admissions McDonough School of Business- Georgetown University The Assistant Director, Graduate & Executive Degree Programs Admissions, supports all activities related to the smooth and effective recruitment and enrollment of incoming students for our graduate and executive degree programs, in particular the Master of Science in Management program. The Assistant Director of Recruitment and Admissions is responsible for all aspects of recruiting outreach including answering emails, telephone calls and walk-in inquiries for the graduate and executive degree programs. He/she/they will implement all procedures for recruiting outreach and follow-up with prospects as well as engaging, cultivating and managing the recruiting pipeline. In addition, the Assistant Director of Recruitment and Admissions will work with the Director to identify opportunities to maximize recruitment for the Master of Science in Management program. Working with the Director, he/she/they will plan recruiting events such as on and off campus information sessions, online information sessions and occasionally travel to represent McDonough at recruiting events and fairs.   The Assistant Director will also serve as the team’s secondary point of contact for admissions operations across all graduate and executive degree programs. In this role, he/she/they will support the Director with creation of and updates to admissions policies and processes, ensuring updates are encoded into manuals and materials. He/she/they will manage student records in Ellucian Banner and support process flows between Salesforce and Ellucian Banner and create dashboards and reports in Salesforce for admissions operations. The Assistant Director will work on annual updates to graduate and executive degree applications and provide administrative support for functions within the team’s meeting and interview scheduling tool, including onboarding new users into the platform.   Additional duties include, but are not limited to: C ommunicate via email, phone, and in-person with prospective Master of Science in Management students Cultivate and manage the recruitment pipeline for the Master of Science in Management program Plan and host recruitment events Update manuals and assist in operational tasks with student data reporting and the meeting scheduling tool. Work Interactions The Assistant Director, Graduate & Executive Degree Programs Admissions reports directly to the Director, Graduate and Executive Degree Programs Admissions and works closely with the Assistant and Associate Deans. This position interacts regularly with external partners, such as prospective students, alumni, Georgetown University offices, as well as working with an Assistant Director and four Associate Directors.   This role directly contributes to the University’s mission by supporting the recruitment and admissions, and therefore revenue generation, for a critical graduate degree program, the Master of Science in Management. Requirements and Qualificat ions Bachelor’s degree required At least 3-5 years’ experience within a corporate or university setting required. Extremely strong interpersonal abilities and strong team orientation required. Must be able to work with various constituencies including prospective students, current students, alumni, faculty, and staff. Substantial working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint required. Preferred qualifications Experience in higher education admissions is strongly preferred. Marketing and events related experience is highly desirable. Comfort with working in excel and analyzing data is a plus. Prior exposure to marketing tasks is a plus. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https:// hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $44,022.00 - $73,406.80 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/2115-Wisconsin-Avenue/Human-Resources-Policy---Procedures-Specialist_JR27579-1": {
      "title": "Human Resources Policy & Procedures Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Human Resources Policy & Procedures Specialist will serve as the strategic lead and subject matter expert on all aspects of HR Policy and Compliance and has the ability to influence, design, and direct  business processes as statutory regulations may require. The incumbent will be responsible for leading a broad portfolio of projects that ensure the practices and procedures across all campuses and departments conform to University Human Resources policy as well as local and federal regulations.  The individual in this role will be responsible for driving the regular assessment of existing policy and practices and the strategic development of new HR policies and procedures including the areas of statutory compliance, reporting, and document management. Additionally, this role will proactively identify compliance risks and provide critical risk-mitigation guidance to university leadership.   Work Interactions The Human Resources Policy & Procedures Specialist will work closely and strategically partner with colleagues in all areas of HR (including, but not limited to HR Business Partners, Classification and Compensation, HCM, Talent Acquisition, and Benefits) to identify opportunities for developing robust techniques and procedures that support compliance at all stages of the employment cycle.   The Human Resources Policy & Procedures Specialist will partner with HCM Services on the review of the work performed by HRCs outside of central Human Resources and provides review/recommendations and high-level strategic direction to HCM Services team and trainer(s) on compliance training programs, including, but not limited to, ensuring compliance with employment regulations in all states where the University is an employer of record.   The Human Resources Policy & Procedures Specialist will also serve as HR’s primary authority and point of contact for University Departments with oversight responsibilities for other regulatory responsibilities, including, but not limited to, working with university stakeholders, legal counsel, and individual departments on matters ranging from FMLA to unemployment, and protection of minors.   Requirements and Qualifications The successful candidate for this position should hold a bachelor’s degree and have 5 to 7 years of broad-based human resources and compliance experience. Advanced knowledge of human resources policies, regulatory requirements and best practices for employment records maintenance and management is an essential element of the work performed in this role. Candidates should also have demonstrated experience managing and directing large-scale projects serving diverse constituencies. Superior writing skills are essential for success. The ability to stay informed on changing regulatory obligations and proactively analyze and mitigate their impact on the University is also necessary. Preference may be granted to candidates with prior policy and compliance experience in a large organization. Candidates must possess strong analytical and communication skills, as well as technical facility with HRIS systems and databases. Prior experience with Workday is preferred.   Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $54,616.00 - $100,493.33 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
