    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Finance-Manager--Prisons-and-Justice-Initiative---Georgetown-University_JR26329": {
      "title": "Finance Manager, Prisons and Justice Initiative – Georgetown University",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Finance Manager (a one-year renewable term position) performs complex financial functions requiring advanced knowledge of university policies, external regulations, and financial systems. This position is responsible for managing and analyzing the financial operations of the Prisons and Justice Initiative (PJI), including budgets, forecasts, grant compliance, and financial reporting. The role conducts financial analyses and prepares recommendations to support strategic decision-making, ensure compliance, and improve financial processes. The Finance Manager serves as the primary financial resource for PJI and represents the unit in coordination with university financial offices. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Managing and monitoring program/organizational budgets and financial activity. Preparing financial analyses, forecasts, and reports for leadership. Ensuring compliance with university financial policies and sponsored project requirements. Overseeing financial transactions and reconciliation processes. Coordinating with university financial offices on complex financial matters. Supporting financial planning and advising leadership on resource allocation. Work Interactions The Finance Manager reports to the Managing Director. This position works closely with PJI leadership, program staff, and central university offices including Main Campus and College Finance, Sponsored Projects Finance Office, Joint Office of Research Administration, and Payroll. The Finance Manager coordinates with university regarding complex financial matters and represents PJI in meetings related to financial operations, compliance, and budgeting. Requirements and Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, or a related field. 3–5 years of professional experience in financial analysis, accounting, or financial management. Demonstrated experience analyzing budgets, financial statements, and financial data. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel (pivot tables, vlookups, financial modeling). Strong knowledge of financial systems, reporting, and compliance requirements. Ability to interpret and apply institutional policies and financial regulations. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills.   Preferred Qualifications Experience working with Workday financial systems. Prior financial experience at Georgetown University or similar higher education environment. Experience with sponsored project financial management, grant reporting, and compliance. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Cover letter and resume required for consideration. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/District-of-Columbia/Security-Officer--Multiple-Opportunities-_JR27740": {
      "title": "Security Officer (Multiple Opportunities)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Position: P158869 Full-time: 40 hours Pay: $21.50 Location: Washington. DC The incumbent maintains the integrity of assigned buildings or areas by understanding access control systems, circulation and safety systems, and emergency exits in event of an emergency. Aware of and understands all special and general orders pertaining to area, building or functions of job. Inspects and reports security and safety of area or building through the use of roving checks and stationary posts. Reports all deficiencies to their supervisor. Knowledge of traffic flow. Recognizes unusual incidents or unwarranted intrusion and effects prompt and proper requests for assistance when required. Utilizes communications available for reporting purposes. Performs other duties as assigned. The incumbent may be assigned to either the Hilltop or Capitol Campus. Work Interactions This position reports to the Police Sergeant. The incumbent works independently with general supervision.  Works with patrol officers, communications dispatchers, security officers, and student guards. Also, interacts routinely with students, faculty, staff, visitors, and the neighboring community. The incumbent is one of the “faces” of the Georgetown University Police Department.   Requirements and Qualifications High School diploma (or equivalent) required. At least 1 year of general work experience is required. Must be legally authorized to work in the United States Must be at least 18 years of age. Must qualify for a Security Officer License in the District of Columbia. Must possess and maintain a valid driver’s license with no violations in the last five years and must be able to pass Georgetown University Driver’s Certification. All applicants are subject to a written test, a report writing test, drug test, physical examination by a medical doctor to University specifications, and extensive psychological testing. Must be able to pass a comprehensive background investigation. Must possess tact, patience, a professional and courteous demeanor, and be customer service-oriented in order to assist students, staff, faculty, visitors, and community members. Must respect the use of licensed authority powers in relation to a University environment. Must possess basic computer skills. Proficient verbal and written communications skills, including report writing, are essential. Preferred Requirements and Qualifications 1 year of security, law enforcement or military experience is preferred, but not required.   Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus . Please note that work-mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .   Position is considered essential under the University Personnel policy guidelines and therefore is subject to be on call when necessary. Must be willing to work extended, odd, or off hours to achieve the expectations of the Department.  This may include rotating tours of duty (day shifts, evening shifts, overnight shifts) with fluctuating days off, according to departmental needs. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
