    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Director-of-Research_JR27848": {
      "title": "Director of Research",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Beeck Center for Social Impact + Innovation at Georgetown University is dedicated to improving how people experience government by strengthening the design and delivery of public services. As a nonprofit, nonpartisan center, we catalyze cross-sector collaboration to advance people-first, digitally-enabled approaches through applied research, peer learning, and hands-on support—helping government deliver better outcomes for communities. The Beeck Center is seeking a Director of Research to lead, scale, and mature the Center’s expanding research offering. The Director will refine the strategic direction, operational systems, and methodologies that define how the Beeck Center conducts and disseminates high-quality, practical, and ethical applied research driven by the real-world challenges governments face today. The research offering focuses on critical topics related to digital transformation of government service delivery, including human-centered design, product management, data governance, artificial intelligence, public benefits, and institutional capacity building. The Beeck Center’s research focuses on sensemaking that informs action, and the Networks team often identifies research topics using our flywheel working model. This is a senior leadership role that combines strategic research design, systems thinking, and program execution, with a heavy emphasis on cross-functional collaboration, ethical research frameworks, and impact assessment. The Director will be responsible for translating field-level practitioner insights into scalable research initiatives, establishing robust quality control standards, including participant protections and data management standards, and defining and delivering on the distinctive applied research approaches that position the Beeck Center as a trusted authority in the public interest technology ecosystem.   Before submitting your application to Georgetown University, visit the Beeck Center’s careers page to learn more about the recruiting process, timeline, and supplemental application requirements.     Work Interactions The Director of Research reports directly to the Beeck Center’s Executive Director. The Director collaborates extensively with other members of the Leadership Team, Fellows, and staff across the organization. The Director directly manages a portfolio team of research staff, contractors, and Student Analysts. The research team works cross-functionally across all central Beeck Center teams, including Networks, Training + Technical Assistance, Operations, Business Development, and Communications, to co-create insights and align program deliverables. The Director will serve as a primary spokesperson for the Center's research portfolio and represent the Beeck Center and Georgetown University publicly, including at conferences, with philanthropic funders, and in media or academic engagements.   The Beeck Center has two office spaces in Washington, D.C.: one on Georgetown University’s Main Campus and a second downtown on Georgetown’s Capitol Campus. We prioritize spending time in person with our student analysts for collaboration and career development as well as building relations across the various other centers on campus. Remote employees will have the opportunity to, and are expected to, travel up to 10% for team retreats, conferences, and in-person workweeks. The Beeck Center operates as a distributed team, with some team members working remotely and others working in-person in our Washington, DC offices. A distributed team means there will be heavy reliance on asynchronous communication channels such as Slack, Asana, and Gmail, while also having many meetings fully virtual or hybrid to include remote employees, using Zoom.     Requirements and Qualifications Education + Experience: Bachelor's degree and 8 or more years of relevant professional experience OR equivalent experience Applied Research Expertise: Proven track record designing and directing applied research initiatives within policy, public administration, data science, civic technology, or related social impact fields. Methodological Framework Design: Deep knowledge of research design principles, qualitative/quantitative methodologies, ethical and equitable research practices, human-subject protection, and Institutional Review Board (IRB) regulations. Strategic Program Leadership: Proven ability to build operational infrastructure from the ground up, manage multi-stakeholder portfolios, coordinate across matrixed functions, and navigate organizational ambiguity. Advanced Communication + Synthesis: Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with a demonstrated ability to translate technical or academic concepts into clear, actionable prose tailored for policymakers, public sector executives, and general audiences. Management & Mentorship: Experience supervising professional staff and contractors, creating effective environments for collaboration and review, and providing dedicated mentorship to students. Values + Approach: Strong commitment to centering equity, serving the public interest, and building public trust in government through rigorous, evidence-driven insights. Tools + Technology: Proficiency utilizing collaborative project management software, asynchronous communication systems, and modern digital publishing or analytics platforms (e.g., Asana, Slack, Zoom, Google Workspace).   Preferred Experience Graduate degree in public policy, public administration, human-centered design, or a related technology and society discipline. Experience working with or within federal, state, or local government agencies, or deep familiarity with service delivery, technology modernization, and procurement in public-sector contexts. Extensive public speaking, publishing, advocacy, and/or academic citation track record within the public interest technology ecosystem. Experience applying accessibility standards (e.g., WCAG) and universal design principles to digital publications and interactive data assets. Experience supervising and developing a team Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Remote. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $80,429.00 - $157,238.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Medical-Center/Senior-Research-Assistant_JR27811-1": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Senior Research Assistant will be a part of the Huntington’s Disease Care Education and Research Center (HD CERC) to assist with clinical trial implementation and clinic scheduling and operations. The position will work independently to implement and run day to day operations for clinical trials in the Huntington’s Center. In addition, the position will require administrative work for the Director of the Center, Clinical Trials Director, and Outreach Coordinator, including independent work with confidential patient files. Work Interactions In addition to reporting to the Clinical Trials Director, the position will work closely with the Research Manager. The candidate will work closely with the Clinical Research Unit (CRU) and other university departments (e.g. MRI, ophthalmology) to ensure protocols are understood and visits there are conducted properly. The candidate will interact closely with study sponsors (Huntington Study Group, pharmaceutical companies, foundations, etc) to maintain GCP and protocol compliance. Requirements and Qualifications Candidate should have a Bachelor’s Degree and at least 1 year of experience in clinical trials working with adult participants. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid 2 Days. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Managers for Hybrid and On-Campus positions may also submit requests to post a salary range following the parameters listed above, but posting this information is not required. Sponsored Project Management (if applicable) If this position serves as the Department Financial Manager for a Sponsored Project, please insert the text found on the HR website:http://hr.georgetown.edu/employment_services/costcentermanagers.html Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $41,926.00 - $65,090.00 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Director--Global-Academic-Programs-and-Partnership-McDonough-School-of-Business_JR27541": {
      "title": "Director, Global Academic Programs and Partnership-McDonough School of Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Director, Global Academic Programs and Partnership, McDonough School of Business- Georgetown University   The Director of Global Academic Programs and Partnerships provides school-wide leadership for MSB’s global academic portfolio and experiential learning programs, ensuring alignment with the school’s mission to develop globally minded business leaders and maintain a competitive international footprint. The Director oversees the full lifecycle of global academic partnerships and global programming—including MBA exchange partnerships, international university relationships, and the Global Business Experience (GBE). This position combines strategic academic partnership development with operational excellence in delivering high-impact, student-facing global programs. MSB sends over 900 students abroad annually across more than 24 GBE sections in 15+ countries, spanning undergraduate, specialized master’s, and MBA programs. The Director ensures these programs are academically rigorous, operationally seamless, and aligned with institutional strategy.   Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Providing strategic oversight for academic components of the Global Business Experience Conducting benchmarking and competitive analysis to inform MSB’s global strategy Managing international university relationships and representing MSB abroad Coordinating global academic initiatives across MSB programs Leading MSB’s global academic partnership strategy, including MBA exchange development Work Interactions The Director reports directly to the Associate Dean for Global Strategic Planning and Operations, and Director of Global Programs. The role works closely with the Academic Director of the Global Business Experience, Senior Associate Dean of MBA Programs, Associate Dean of MBA Programs, MBA Program Office, Undergraduate Program Office, MSB Finance, Office of Global Education, Office of International Safety & Security, Student Health Insurance, and the Office of Global Services. The Director interacts regularly with international university partners, global vendors, U.S. Embassy officials abroad, corporate partners, alumni, and faculty leads across all MSB programs. This role directly contributes to the University’s mission by strengthening MSB’s global academic partnerships, enhancing the school’s global reputation, and ensuring the delivery of academically rigorous, globally engaged programs. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree required, preferably in international business, higher education administration, global affairs, or related field 5-7 years in academic program management, global partnerships, or international education Demonstrated experience developing and managing international academic partnerships Strong analytical skills, including benchmarking and competitive analysis Proven ability to manage complex global academic initiatives and risk considerations Excellent communication skills and intercultural fluency Proficiency with Microsoft Office and data management tools       Preferred qualifications Master’s Degree Preferred Foreign language proficiency preferred Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $66,783.00 - $126,720.23 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Seasonal-Application-Reader-3--Part--Time--Temporary_JR27793": {
      "title": "Seasonal Application Reader-3, Part- Time, Temporary",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Seasonal Application Reader supports the Office of Undergraduate Admissions by conducting comprehensive, holistic reviews of undergraduate applications within a highly selective admissions environment. This role is critical to ensuring that each applicant is evaluated thoughtfully, consistently, and in alignment with Georgetown’s institutional values, admissions philosophy, and established review standards. Readers are responsible for assessing a wide range of academic and contextual factors, including curriculum rigor, academic achievement, extracurricular engagement, personal qualities, and the opportunities available to each applicant. The position requires strong analytical judgment, the ability to synthesize complex information, and a deep commitment to fairness, consistency, and confidentiality. Readers must quickly develop an understanding of Georgetown’s evaluative framework and apply it consistently across a large volume of applications. This is a part-time position, working a maximum of 20 hours per week during the application review period between October and March. Work is primarily conducted remotely using a web-based admissions information system, with required participation in training and calibration sessions. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Conduct holistic, contextual reviews of undergraduate applications using Georgetown’s admissions criteria Evaluate academic preparation, intellectual curiosity, and personal contributions within context Apply institutional standards consistently across all assigned applications Prepare clear, concise, and well-supported written evaluations Participate in training and calibration to ensure alignment with review standards Maintain strict confidentiality and data integrity Meet productivity expectations and adhere to review timelines Work Interactions The Seasonal Application Reader works closely with the Office of Undergraduate Admissions and reports to a designated Senior Associate or Associate Director. The role contributes directly to the university’s selection process by providing critical evaluative input on applicants. Readers collaborate indirectly with admissions staff by ensuring consistency and quality in application review and may receive ongoing feedback to calibrate evaluations. This position supports Georgetown University’s mission to enroll a diverse and academically talented student body aligned with its values of intellectual rigor, service, and global engagement. Requirements and Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required Demonstrated ability to analyze and synthesize complex information Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Ability to manage time effectively and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment High-level of discretion and ability to maintain confidentiality Proficiency with technology and ability to learn new systems quickly Reliable internet access and secure, private workspace Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in college counseling, admissions, application review, or related higher education Experience working with the Slate admissions system Familiarity with holistic admissions practices Conflicts of Interest and Eligibility Requirements To ensure the integrity, fairness, and confidentiality of Georgetown University’s admissions process, Seasonal Application Readers must adhere to strict conflict-of-interest guidelines. Individuals are not eligible for this position if they: Are a parent, guardian, or immediate family member of a current high school junior or senior, regardless of whether the student intends to apply to Georgetown University Are currently employed as a high school or college counselor, independent educational consultant, or in any admissions-related role Are employed by, or serve in an advising capacity for, another undergraduate degree-granting institution Have any personal, professional, or financial relationship that could reasonably be perceived as influencing the impartial evaluation of applicants All current Georgetown employees are not eligible for this position. All Seasonal Application Readers are required to: Disclose any actual, potential, or perceived conflicts of interest prior to and during employment Recuse themselves from the review of any application where a conflict exists Maintain strict confidentiality regarding all applicant information and admissions deliberations, in accordance with Georgetown University policies Failure to comply with conflict-of-interest and confidentiality expectations may result in immediate termination of employment. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation.  Pay Range   The projected hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $23.50 - $27.50. Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
