    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Medical-Center/Teaching-Assistant---Temporary_JR27933": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant - Temporary",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The position is a Teaching Assistant for the Department of Neuroscience in the Georgetown University Medical Center. The course is Basic Neuroscience I, which is a two hour course that meets twice a week (Mondays and Wednesdays). There are over 30 graduate students enrolled (both MS and PhD). There are a lot of aspects of the course – recorded lectures, quizzes most weeks, exams four times during the semester, in-class assignments, short in-class lectures periodically (6-7 times per semester), other in-class events, and review sessions. A Teaching Assistant could help with some small aspects of each of these aspects, depending on their knowledge and availability. It would be particularly useful is the candidate had taken Basic Neuroscience I in a previous year. It is not necessary for the Teaching Assistant to have prior experience teaching.   Additional duties include but are not limited to: Answer specific questions from students (email or outside of class) Help grade exams Run part of review sessions during the semester Give one in-class lecture (less than 15 minutes) Run Cahoots or Jeopardy events Work with the faculty to identify any students who are struggling   Work Interactions The Teaching Assistant would report to the Course Director regarding each of the duties. The position is necessary due to the heavy teaching load for a four-credit course with a large number of students. The faculty are tenured Professors in the Department of Neuroscience. This position allows more individual attention to the students from both the Teaching Assistant and the Professors.   Requirements and Qualifications A successful applicant would: Have a MS or high degree in Neuroscience or a closely related field Have a good general knowledge of Neuroscience Be comfortable speaking in front of a class Be comfortable using classroom software such as Canvas.     Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .  Pay Range   The projected hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $21.64 - $26.44. Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Program-Manager--Racial-Justice-Institute---Georgetown-University_JR27927-1": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Racial Justice Institute - Georgetown University",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Program Manager, Racial Justice Institute – Georgetown University provides high-level program and operational support to advance the research initiatives, academic publications, and strategic partnerships led by Dr. Evelyn Patterson, Faculty Director of the Racial Justice Institute (RJI).  RJI is an academic initiative focused on interdisciplinary scholarship and programming designed to cultivate the connective tissue that dissolves institutional silos and amplify racial justice research.   This role balances operational execution, stakeholder and faculty coordination, event management, and research project tracking across RJI’s interdisciplinary work on campus, particularly at the intersection of the social sciences, law, and medicine. The Program Manager is the primary administrative professional supporting the work of RJI and will also provide support on routine business processes including coordination with colleagues in finance, procurement, human resources, and the Office of the Provost.   Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Provide operational support for RJI including, but not limited to, project management, academic research support, record keeping and database management, and execution of basic business processes. Coordinate with faculty, undergraduate and graduate students, visiting scholars, internal Georgetown departments/schools/centers/institutes, and external research partners. Lead the planning, logistics, and execution of academic events, research symposia, policy workshops, guest lectures, and panel discussions. Work closely with Institutional Partnerships and Strategy Development team and the Office of the Provost to support efforts to secure and steward research funding initiatives and joint projects. Work Interactions The Program Manager role reports directly to Dr. Evelyn Patterson, Professor, McCourt School of Public Policy and Faculty Director, Racial Justice Institute. This role will be a key contact for campus colleagues as well as external partners to facilitate the research ambitions of RJI. Strong written and verbal communications skills and the ability to work across departments is essential. This role requires independent decision making, strong judgement, and the ability to manage multiple workflows.   Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and two years of relevant experience in in research administration, program management, academic operations, or stakeholder coordination required. Background in the social sciences, law, and/or public health/medicine, alongside research experience. Demonstrated familiarity with academic formatting, citation systems, and manuscript preparation preferred. Experience or strong interest in translating research findings into products such as policy briefs, academic reports, digital products, and actionable deliverables a plus.    Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
