    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/ICC-2nd-Floor/Executive-Director-of-External-Relations-and-Marketing--Walsh-School-of-Foreign-Service--SFS-_JR27445": {
      "title": "Executive Director of External Relations and Marketing, Walsh School of Foreign Service (SFS)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements The Walsh School of Foreign Service (SFS), founded in 1919, is a premier school of international relations. At Georgetown’s Washington, D.C. and Qatar campuses, SFS provides a rigorous education combining theory and practice and instills the values of service.  The School's liberal arts undergraduate program, leading to the Bachelor of Science in Foreign Service, includes a two-year required core curriculum followed by two years of multidisciplinary electives. Eight interdisciplinary graduate programs are designed to teach students to think, analyze and act with imagination, good judgment and compassion.  The vision of the School is to contribute to global peace, prosperity and human well-being by educating future generations of world leaders and expanding the knowledge, understanding and values that will inform their leadership. The Executive Director of External Relations and Marketing will plan and direct a strategic and effective communications and external relations program for the School that increases stakeholder engagement and public interest in the School, and enhances the image of the School.  This will include overseeing the School’s communications and events team, and the external relations staff and outreach activities of the School.  The Executive Director will provide strategic leadership to the constituent academic units of the School on all matters relating to communications and external relations, with the aim of ensuring consistency and efficiency in the development and delivery of all communications and in engagement with stakeholders.  The Executive Director will develop and implement a strategic marketing campaign to increase applications to SFS undergraduate and graduate programs with particular attention to strengthening our international and under-represented applicant pool. The Executive Director will strengthen our outreach to the SFS alumni community including regular communications on campus happenings, fast-break analysis from SFS faculty in response to global issues, and specially tailored alumni events in key alumni markets. The Executive Director will work with SFS faculty to promote their research on areas of interest to the policy community. The Executive Director will have oversight for conceptualization and implementation of signature and/or stakeholder-focused events related to the School. The Executive Director will also engage University officials to include the Office of the GU President, Chairs, Deans and Directors on matters pertaining to communications, marketing, and event planning for the school. The Executive Director will also be expected to strengthen the School’s engagement with the broader Washington, DC policy, multilateral, and business communities ensuring topical and high-profile visits from policymakers and practitioners to campus and strategic outreach on key global issues. Reporting to the Dean, the Executive Director of External Relations and Marketing will be a member of the School's senior leadership team, participating in critical decisions and advising the Dean on important matters related to the School and the School’s role in the broader policy dialogue.  The Executive Director will play a key advisory role in developing strategies for those areas that impact the stakeholder experience.  The Executive Director supervises the School’s Director of Communications, Director of Events and Alumni Engagement, and Web Content Producer. Minimum requirements include a Bachelor’s degree in public relations, communications, marketing, higher education administration, or related field, and at least 10 years of progressively responsible experience in communications and/or external relations, preferably in higher education, government, multilateral or policy-related institutions, including 5 years of supervisory experience (or equivalent combination of education and work experience). Master’s degree preferred. A broad and up-to-date understanding of communications and external relations strategies is expected. Knowledge of the Washington DC institutional landscape is desirable. The successful candidate will have exceptional writing and presentational skills as well as demonstrated ability to organize teams to achieve results, and the ability to quickly garner credibility and develop and maintain relationships with a wide variety of internal and external stakeholders. A high level of organizational competence and effective time management is expected.  This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $103,723.00 - $202,778.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/125-E-St-NW-5th-Floor/Research-Finance---Operations-Coordinator---McCourt-School-of-Public-Policy---Georgetown-University_JR27899": {
      "title": "Research Finance & Operations Coordinator - McCourt School of Public Policy - Georgetown University",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Research Finance & Operations Coordinator provides essential administrative, financial and human capital management (HCM) execution for the McCourt School of Public Policy's Research Enterprise. Reporting directly to the Senior Director of Research Finance, this position serves as a core operational bridge for a growing portfolio of research centers, faculty and research teams spread across campus locations. Working alongside Research Administration Managers (RAMs) and the broader School finance team, the Research Finance & Operations Coordinator handles frontline operations, initiates research personnel and student hiring workflows, executes transactional financial processes, and maintains efficient day-to-day financial operations. This role offers high visibility into the full life cycle of sponsored research and center management within a high-volume and dynamic research environment. Key Duties & Responsibilities HR Administration & Research Personnel Personnel Workflows: Initiate and track HCM processing, E-requests, appointment letters, and onboarding workflows for all research personnel types—including research faculty, staff, post-doctoral fellows, temporary employees, visiting scholars, research fellows, and research affiliates. Student Employment: Coordinate the recruitment, hiring, onboarding, and hourly timekeeping processing for grant-supported student workers across McCourt research centers. Administrative Liaison: Serve as the primary operational liaison with central administrative offices—including the Dean’s Office, Provost Office HCM team, Office of Faculty Affairs, Student Employment Office and Office for Global Services—to resolve visa, payroll, and other HCM paperwork. Research Financial & Operational Transactions Financial Processing: Execute day-to-day transactional financial workflows across 145+ active grant accounts, contracts, and center funds, including purchase orders, procurement contracts, miscellaneous payment requests, expense reimbursements (employee and procard) and GU Travel processing, subaward support documents, ACH forms, etc. Financial Monitoring: Support the Senior Director and RAMs in routine financial monitoring of internal and external funds by compiling expenditure data, tracking payments, preparing journals, and assisting with monthly ledger reconciliations of suspense accounts and institutional accounts. Student Financial Operations: Assist with student financial processing where applicable, including tracking grant-funded tuition merit aid, work study credits, research stipends and costing allocations. Research Operations & General Administration Office & Tech Operations: Maintain day-to-day office operations for the McCourt Research Enterprise including facilities, supplies, and technology service requests (e.g., cell phone management and computer orders). Constituent Contact: Act as a professional primary point of contact for internal and external constituents, answering faculty and student inquiries with high-quality, customer-service-oriented communication. Process Improvement: Identify opportunities to streamline internal administrative procedures, operational protocols, and office workflows across the research centers.Work Interactions Direct Team: Reports directly to the Senior Director of Research Finance and works in daily partnership with Research Administration Managers (RAMs), Grants and Contracts Accountant, and the McCourt Finance team. Internal Stakeholders: Interacts regularly with McCourt center directors, PIs, research faculty and staff across all locations. External/University Support Units: Liaises frequently with the Office of Faculty Affairs (OFA), Provost HCM, Facilities, Procurement, Joint Office for Research Administration (JORA), Sponsored Projects Financial Operations (SPFO) and Student Employment (SEO). Requirements and Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Experience: Minimum 2 years of administrative and operational experience in a professional office environment, preferably within higher education, a research enterprise, or a non-profit setting. Technical Skills: Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, PowerPoint) with intermediate-to-advanced Excel skills (basic formulas, spreadsheet management). Preferred Qualifications Direct experience handling personnel hiring workflows, student employment processing, or basic accounts payable/procurement transactions. Familiarity with university enterprise systems (e.g., Workday/GMS, Cognos) and general higher education administrative policies. Basic understanding of sponsored research environments. Exceptional organizational skills, high attention to detail, strong problem-solving abilities, and a service-oriented approach to collaborating with faculty and senior administrators. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $44,022.00 - $73,406.80 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/125-E-St-NW-1st-Floor/Policy-Director--Economic-Dignity-Lab---McCourt-School-of-Public-Policy---Georgetown-University_JR27896": {
      "title": "Policy Director, Economic Dignity Lab - McCourt School of Public Policy - Georgetown University",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Part-Time Policy Director, Economic Dignity Lab, McCourt School of Public Policy - Georgetown University. The Economic Dignity Lab develops evidence-based policy proposals focused on ensuring all Americans have the ability to provide for loved ones, pursue purpose and potential, and work with respect and dignity. The Policy Director will work with the Executive Director on the substantive development of the Lab’s policy agenda, setting research priorities, shepherding work by research assistants, consultants and coauthors on publications, and working to develop public events presentations that help present the Lab’s work to policymakers, academics, and the public. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Supporting the development of the Lab’s policy agenda, major policy papers, briefs, and reports from conception through publication Supervising and mentoring research assistants and student researchers and guiding their day-to-day research work Coordinating the work of outside policy experts and contributing authors Contributing to the Lab’s public forums and events Work Interactions The Policy Director reports directly to the Founding Executive Director of the Economic Dignity Lab and works in close partnership with the Managing Director on the Lab’s operations and output. The position provides substantive direction to the Lab’s research assistants and student researchers and collaborates with commissioned policy experts, McCourt School faculty, and external partners in government, academia, and the advocacy community. As the senior substantive lead on the Lab’s policy work, the Policy Director will work with the Executive Director to shape the intellectual direction of the Lab’s publications and ensure they meet the highest standards of rigor and impact. The role advances Georgetown University’s commitment to empowering people in service of others by producing research that seeks tangible policy impact on the economic well-being of workers and families across the nation. Requirements and Qualifications Preference of  five years of progressively responsible experience in policy development, analysis, or a related field, ideally in government, academia, think tanks, or advocacy organizations Demonstrated ability to author and edit rigorous, publication-quality policy papers and briefs Capacity to exhibit serious substantive knowledge on  the Lab’s focus areas, such as labor markets, AI and the future of work, job creation, workforce development, care policy, and tax policy Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to translate complex analysis for policymaker and public audiences Strong project management skills and the ability to manage multiple publications and deadlines simultaneously Experience supervising or mentoring junior researchers Commitment to at least 15-20 hours per week Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in public policy, economics, law, or a related field; advanced degree (Master’s, JD, or PhD) in public policy, economics, law, or a related field valued Prior experience in federal or state policymaking, including work in the executive branch, Congress, or state government Established network among policymakers, researchers, and advocates in economic and labor policy Familiarity with the economic dignity framework and the Lab’s body of work   Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $64.99 - $127.06 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
