    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/2115-Wisconsin-Avenue/Chief-of-Staff---Director-of-Special-Projects_JR27974": {
      "title": "Chief of Staff & Director of Special Projects",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview This position serves as a multifaceted leader within the Georgetown University Medical Center’s (GUMC) team, bridging the gap between high-level constituent engagement and strategic administrative oversight. Reporting to the Vice President for GUMC Advancement, the Chief of Staff and Director of Special Projects will serve as a key convener, collaborator, and project manager for the GUMC Advancement team, which is working to advance and secure significant philanthropic support for Georgetown’s Medical Center. This position plays a pivotal role in multiple core functional areas such as accelerating administrative functions in GUMC Advancement, serving as a key liaison with the EVP’s office, assisting the VP for GUMC Advancement in the day-to-day oversight of the GUMC Advancement team’s activities, and managing the team’s budget oversight and spending discretion. The Chief of Staff will also serve as the primary Clinical Patient Navigator for the newly established \"GUMC GPS\" program, providing white-glove, concierge-level support for referred patients into the GUMC/MedStar Health partnership. This role also oversees the financial and compliance integrity of the Medical Center’s current use and endowed philanthropic funds, working closely with GUMC’s EVP’s office, advancement leadership, school and unit senior business managers (SBMs), and academic department heads to ensure philanthropic dollars are financially stewarded with precision and transparency. Lastly, with alignment and direction from the VP, this role leads the planning and execution of GUMC Advancement initiatives and special projects that are a strategic priority for GUMC. This work will include communicating project details, building and tracking against timelines, and raising challenges to both internal and external stakeholders to ensure progress is achieved.  A successful candidate possesses exceptional diplomatic skills, financial acumen, and the ability to operate in a high-stakes, confidential environment.   Duties include but are not limited to:  Serve as the Chief of Staff and strategic advisor to the VP for GUMC Advancement, and key operational driver for GUMC Advancement priorities and day-to-day oversight; lead cross-functional strategic initiatives, and ensure high-priority business goals are effectively executed. Serve as the primary Clinical Patient Navigator for the newly established GUMC GPS program. Oversee financial stewardship and compliance for GUMC current use and endowed philanthropic funds.  Lead the planning and execution of initiatives and special projects as directed by the VP for GUMC Advancement.   Work Interactions This position integrates complex administrative, financial, and patient-navigation workflows within the Office of the Executive Vice President to support GUMC's operational and strategic goals. The role reports directly to the GUMC VP of Advancement and maintains a dotted reporting line to the Managing Director of GUMC Operations and Strategic Engagement for the initial GPS program launch. The role interfaces extensively with MedStar clinical staff, GUMC department heads, advancement leadership, senior business managers, and Faculty Affairs. This position will also collaborate with the centralized Office of Advancement teams, including Stewardship, Communications, Annual Fund, Alumni Engagement, DATA, Prospect Management, Revenue Management, Campaign Operations, Special Events, Donor Events, and Engagement. By fostering a positive workplace culture and ensuring seamless navigation for high-profile constituents, this position directly supports GUMC’s broader mission of research, teaching, service, and patient care, which is rooted in the Jesuit principle of cura personalis.   Requirements and Qualifications ·        Education: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Healthcare Administration, Human Resources, or a related field. ·        Experience: 10+ years of overall professional experience with a minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible experience in executive administration, strategic project management, or healthcare navigation within a highly complex environment. ·        Technical Qualifications: Proficiency in financial tracking tools, Microsoft Office and Google Workspace, and a thorough understanding of HIPAA-compliant communication protocols. ·        Skills: Exceptional diplomatic and interpersonal skills, strong financial acumen, and the proven ability to independently manage special projects, facility logistics, and human resources onboarding while maintaining strict confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications: ·        Prior experience in an academic medical center or higher education environment. ·        Familiarity with philanthropic fund stewardship and endowed faculty appointment processes. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $103,723.00 - $202,778.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
